      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Wedge basics: one graph, one job per row. No model needed.\n\n1. PD Wedge has three rows for the token {size}: 256, 512 and 1024. Its int output feeds Upscale Image's width and height, so each job renders a different size.\n2. Its wedge output goes to PD Output, where {size} names the file: example_256.png, example_512.png, example_1024.png.\n3. Press preview wedge on PD Output to list the paths, then Run: 3 jobs are queued.\n\nTry solo = 2 to render only 512, or chain a second PD Wedge into the first one's wedge input for every combination (see 08). Load one result back with PD Load: its sidecar tells sequence_mode auto it is a single image."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "Wedge basics: one graph, one job per row. No model needed.\n\n1. PD Wedge has three rows for the token {size}: 256, 512 and 1024. Its int output feeds Upscale Image's width and height, so each job renders a different size.\n2. Its wedge output goes to PD Output, where {size} names the file: example_256.png, example_512.png, example_1024.png.\n3. Press preview wedge on PD Output to list the paths, then Run: 3 jobs are queued.\n\nTry solo = 2 to render only 512, or chain a second PD Wedge into the first one's wedge input for every combination (see 08). Load one result back with PD Load: its sidecar tells sequence_mode auto it is a single image."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
